# Change: D-A7 and A-D (repertoire plan: st-change-d-a7-a-d). An original chord-change study.
# Each half is a ladder that changes faster and faster: the home chord D held for two bars (one
# strum a bar), then a change every bar with two strums, every bar with four strums, and every
# two beats. First half: D (xx0232: finger 1 on string 3 fret 2, 3 on string 2 fret 3, 2 on
# string 1 fret 2) with A7 (x02020: finger 2 on string 4 fret 2, 3 on string 2 fret 2), so
# finger 3 slides one fret along string 2. Second half: D with A (x02220), fingered 2-1-3
# (2 on string 4, 1 on string 3, 3 on string 2): finger 1 stays on string 3, fret 2 for both.
# Strum D on strings 4 to 1, A and A7 on strings 5 to 1. Keep the metronome on: the new chord
# lands on the beat even if the strum before it catches open strings. The teacher plays an
# original tune in D whose notes on beats 1 and 3 belong to the chord in force.
title: Change: D-A7 and A-D
id: st-change-d-a7-a-d
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original chord-change study for Sixstring Academy
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 2
tags: chord changes, strumming, metronome, anchor finger, d, a7, a
tempo: 60
time: 4/4
key: D

track: Your strum
role: rhythm
[D and A7]
| ^"One strum a bar" "D=xx0232" w D | D | ^"Two strums a bar" "A7=x02020" h D D | "D=xx0232" D D |
| ^"Four strums a bar" "A7=x02020" q D D D D | "D=xx0232" D D D D | ^"Change every two beats" "A7=x02020" D D "D=xx0232" D D | "A7=x02020" D D "D=xx0232" D D ||
[D and A]
| ^"Finger 1 stays on string 3, fret 2" "D=xx0232" w D | D | ^"Two strums a bar" "A=x02220" h D D | "D=xx0232" D D |
| ^"Four strums a bar" "A=x02220" q D D D D | "D=xx0232" D D D D | ^"Change every two beats" "A=x02220" D D "D=xx0232" D D | "A=x02220" D D "D=xx0232" h D ||

track: Teacher
role: lead
[D and A7]
